# VLAN Configuration Lab

## 📌 Objective

Configure VLANs on a Cisco switch to logically separate network devices into different broadcast domains.

## 🧩 Network Topology

The lab consists of:

* 1 Cisco switch
* Multiple PCs
* VLAN 10 — Sales
* VLAN 20 — IT

## 🌐 VLAN Configuration

| VLAN | Name  | Network         |
| ---- | ----- | --------------- |
| 10   | SALES | 192.168.10.0/24 |
| 20   | IT    | 192.168.20.0/24 |

## ⚙️ Configuration

### Create VLANs

```cisco
Switch# configure terminal

Switch(config)# vlan 10
Switch(config-vlan)# name SALES
Switch(config-vlan)# exit

Switch(config)# vlan 20
Switch(config-vlan)# name IT
Switch(config-vlan)# exit
```

### Assign Ports

```cisco
Switch(config)# interface range fastethernet 0/1-4
Switch(config-if-range)# switchport mode access
Switch(config-if-range)# switchport access vlan 10
Switch(config-if-range)# exit

Switch(config)# interface range fastethernet 0/5-8
Switch(config-if-range)# switchport mode access
Switch(config-if-range)# switchport access vlan 20
Switch(config-if-range)# exit
```

## 🔍 Verification

The following commands can be used to verify the configuration:

```cisco
show vlan brief
show interfaces status
show running-config
```

## ✅ Expected Result

Devices connected to VLAN 10 should belong to the same broadcast domain, while devices connected to VLAN 20 should belong to a separate broadcast domain.

## 📚 Concepts Demonstrated

* VLAN creation
* VLAN naming
* Access ports
* Broadcast domains
* Switch port configuration
* VLAN verification
* Basic Cisco IOS commands

## 🚀 Future Enhancement

The next stage of this lab is to configure **Inter-VLAN Routing** so that devices in VLAN 10 and VLAN 20 can communicate through a router.
